[h1]THE DEEP ANSWERS[/h1]
[i]Call. Feed. Awaken.[/i]

An unofficial, complete summoner path for Vanilla Psycasts Expanded.
Created by Nidelese.

[h2]BECOME THE DEEPCALLER[/h2]

The crust is thinner than anyone realizes.

Call living tentacles up through luminous rifts. Let them hunt, feed and grow. Raise an [b]Idol of the Deep[/b], leave offerings within its shadow, and deepen the god's powers without skipping a tentacle's own growth. When the colony's need becomes great enough, awaken the [b]Leviathan[/b] — one hungry intelligence expressed through a central mantle, eight independently hunting arms and three stunning eye-flowers.

Deepcaller is an area-control path about building a living ecosystem on the battlefield. Its creatures are strange, magical and faintly horrifying — but still very friend-shaped.

[h2]THE LIVING ARSENAL[/h2]

[list]
[*][b]Sprout[/b] — a mobile melee summon with custom idle, sleepy, curl, snap, spiral and recoil animation.
[*][b]Bud[/b] — a rooted ranged evolution. It lasts longer, never leaves its cast square, and fires slow ghostfire whose damage, speed and attack rate grow with Idol devotion.
[*][b]Idol of the Deep[/b] — the heart of the path. Feed it corpses to build devotion, deepen the god's powers and unlock the deep's economy.
[*][b]Cultivate the brood[/b] — spend gold on permanent Bud and melee upgrades. Repeatable upgrades compound in price, while devotion keeps discounting future purchases. Track a goal and see how offerings bring it closer. Purchase "Buds shoot non-organics" to teach the entire ranged brood to fight mechs, golems and hostile machines.
[*][b]A growing god[/b] — devotion awakens new idol titles, living rings and faster digestion. Tentacles drag, cleave and slam as they evolve; mature meals remain useful. Movement cultivation applies to ordinary melee tentacles, preserving the Leviathan's formation.
[*][b]Grasp[/b] — a precise tactical hold. Erupt beneath a victim, leash it to the cast point and drag it back when it tries to escape. Flesh, mechs and golems can all be held.
[*][b]Riptide[/b] — calamity. Turn creatures, vehicles and loose possessions into spontaneous projectiles. Initial pull is strongest at the outer edge; actual travel builds momentum. Acceleration ends at the center, but projectiles coast onward. Air and impacts slow them after crossing; before then, collisions cost HP while the god keeps pushing. A truck, gold bar or unfortunate cow can mine with enough force, taking recoil as it does. Newly dropped loot stays outside the cast. Three separate gold favors spare your walls, your people from being thrown, and your possessions from being thrown. Each requires a sated local idol. Unclaimed chunks still fly, and spared people can still be hit. Buy stronger acceleration or separately extend pull area and cast distance. Unsupported mountain roofs can collapse.
[*][b]Ink Veil[/b] — bloom an animated cloud of abyssal ink that spoils hostile sight and gunfire, coating eyes and mechanical sensors alike.
[*][b]Consume[/b] — the dangerous late-game dismissal. Health, wealth and combat strength determine the heat bill; one powerful boss can make the god eat the caster too. Buy burn reduction and deliberately widen the maw one tile at a time. Greater Devotion makes larger feasts possible.
[*][b]Cultivate the hoard[/b] — permanent gold upgrades improve silver ransom prices, salvage gear from corpse offerings, restore recovered equipment and cleanse corpse-worn apparel. Devotion keeps improving bargains beyond the old final tier.
[*][b]Tideguard[/b] — wrap summons in an animated shell of living water that reacts to impacts and visibly breaks.
[*][b]Leviathan's Wake[/b] — awaken a coordinated organism whose head, flowers and arms retain distinct targeting while moving and hunting as one creature.
[/list]

[h2]THE LEVIATHAN[/h2]

Summon the boss itself to deal with your foes, chase, stun, reduce their defenses, and devour them.


[h1]REQUIRED DEPENDENCIES[/h1]

[b]Deepcaller will not load correctly without all three required mods:[/b]
[list]
[*][url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=2009463077]Harmony[/url]
[*][url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=2023507013]Vanilla Expanded Framework[/url]
[*][url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=2842502659]Vanilla Psycasts Expanded[/url]
[/list]

[b]Also required:[/b] RimWorld 1.6 and the Royalty DLC (required by Vanilla Psycasts Expanded).

[h2]LOAD ORDER[/h2]

Recommended order:
[code]Harmony
Core and DLC
Vanilla Expanded Framework
Vanilla Psycasts Expanded
Vanilla Psycasts Expanded — Deepcaller[/code]

